WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.165
An agent was allowed to act, and the log of that allowance is
intact.

00:00:04.165 --> 00:00:05.614
Most reviews stop there.

00:00:05.614 --> 00:00:11.952
The open question is whether that log warrants the conclusion that
an unauthorized effect did not commit.

00:00:12.602 --> 00:00:17.836
Three readers are about to look at the same record, and only one is
asking that question.

00:00:17.836 --> 00:00:22.071
The first treats an intact actor line as proof the effect was in
bounds.

00:00:22.071 --> 00:00:25.894
The second takes the historical label, the one already published.

00:00:25.894 --> 00:00:29.834
The third asks whether the record is evidence for the effect claim.

00:00:30.484 --> 00:00:35.047
Those three readers are about to be scored, and these two counts
stay apart.

00:00:35.047 --> 00:00:38.348
Forty-eight packets are four views of twelve histories.

00:00:38.348 --> 00:00:42.851
On that set, the two sink views are the twenty-four decisive
opportunities.

00:00:42.851 --> 00:00:46.753
An unsupported support is a support the warrant does not justify.

00:00:46.753 --> 00:00:52.276
The sixteen probes are edits of a single readback. They do not get
added to the forty-eight.

00:00:52.926 --> 00:01:00.486
Trusting the intact actor record overclaims twenty-six times, and
four of those supports are of a false proposition.

00:01:00.486 --> 00:01:04.591
The historical label still carries eleven unsupported supports.

00:01:04.591 --> 00:01:05.960
The checker has none.

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:09.870
Those eleven stay. The zero beside them does not erase them.

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:13.225
The eleven are the ones that look finished.

00:01:13.225 --> 00:01:18.761
The proposition is true, the actor record looks intact, and
admission marks it misbound.

00:01:18.761 --> 00:01:21.026
None of them has a deciding premise.

00:01:21.026 --> 00:01:26.876
Four of the eleven have no effect row, and seven have a withheld
effect row labeled supports.

00:01:26.876 --> 00:01:31.720
A withheld row labeled supports does not explain the four with no
effect row.

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:36.942
This reading does not establish why the retained verdict supported
the other seven.

00:01:36.942 --> 00:01:45.560
A further withheld packet has that same label and is not in the
eleven. Its proposition is false, and the historical label is
unresolved.

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:50.750
On these forty-eight, the intact-actor rule supports every packet.

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:57.421
Rejecting the misbound probe, and still trusting the actor, leaves
fourteen unsupported supports.

00:01:57.421 --> 00:02:02.030
The effect row's own support label still backs a false proposition.

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:11.797
Subject class without the absence census leaves eight warranted
supports unresolved: both sink views of the four histories with no
effect row.

00:02:11.797 --> 00:02:16.474
Subject class, or that zero-row census, matches the full projection.

00:02:17.124 --> 00:02:22.542
Step outside this set, and the checks that were quiet here show up
in the sixteen.

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:26.904
Subject class supports nine that the projection leaves unresolved.

00:02:26.904 --> 00:02:35.163
Those nine are three scope checks, three binding checks, an unknown
subject beside an authorized sink, and two census checks.

00:02:35.163 --> 00:02:40.714
They are a count inside the sixteen. The sixteen stay separate from
the forty-eight.

00:02:40.714 --> 00:02:47.388
An exact duplicate census stays supported, and a sink whose only
subject is unknown stays unresolved.

00:02:48.038 --> 00:02:52.013
On these records, an intact actor log is not the effect warrant.

00:02:52.013 --> 00:02:57.416
On the forty-eight, subject class, or the zero-row absence census,
matches the checker.

00:02:57.416 --> 00:03:00.521
SoundGate's protocol is a separate pair of claims.

00:03:00.521 --> 00:03:05.801
The projection returns supported for the barrier and refuted for the
original policy.

00:03:05.801 --> 00:03:12.446
An intact run record still supports the original policy. The forty-
eight and the sixteen are not this test.
